---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Carbone",
  servesCuisine: ["Italian", "Italian-American"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-702-590-2663",
  url: "https://aria.mgmresorts.com/en/restaurants/carbone.html",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "3730 S Las Vegas Blvd",
    addressLocality: "Las Vegas",
    addressRegion: "NV",
    postalCode: "89158",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Carbone at ARIA Resort & Casino, Las Vegas — Major Food Group's Italian-American fine-dining supper club, led by executive chef Jonah Resnick.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Carbone Las Vegas Menu Guide (2026) — Prices, What to Order | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to Carbone at ARIA Las Vegas: reported prices (spicy rigatoni ~$36, veal parm ~$65), hours, reservations, and visiting tips. Prices reported as of October 2026."
  path="/carbone-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/carbone-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/carbone-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a retro Italian-American supper club with red leather banquettes (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Las Vegas
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Carbone — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The Las Vegas outpost of Major Food Group's 2013 Greenwich Village hit — opened at
      ARIA's Promenade level in October 2015 — Carbone is the Strip's temple of
      Italian-American maximalism: a mid-century supper club designed by Ken Fulk with red
      leather booths, tuxedoed captains, tableside Caesar salads, and a vintage-rum cart.
      Executive chef Jonah Resnick runs the kitchen. It is consistently one of the hardest
      reservations on the Strip (a sibling, Carbone Riviera, opened at Bellagio in late
      2025). Below is our independent walkthrough of the menu with reported prices, hours,
      and what we'd order. Everything is written in our own words; prices below are dated
      public reports, flagged as such — the restaurant publishes no current menu prices.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">3730 S Las Vegas Blvd, Las Vegas, NV 89158 (Promenade level, ARIA Resort &amp; Casino)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive Chef Jonah Resnick</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Italian-American fine dining</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Very expensive — pastas reported $30–$55, mains $50–$75 (mid-2025 reports)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Essential — book via the ARIA site or +1 (702) 590-2663; not on OpenTable's booking network</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Sun–Thu 5:00–10:30 PM; Fri–Sat 5:00–11:00 PM</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Reported on the official ARIA page: <strong>Sunday–Thursday, 5:00–10:30 PM;
        Friday–Saturday, 5:00–11:00 PM</strong>. Dinner only — no lunch service.
      </p>

      <h2>Menu highlights &amp; reported prices</h2>
      <p>
        The restaurant publishes no current prices. The latest dated figures (mid-2025
        reporting): <strong>spicy rigatoni vodka ~$36</strong>, <strong>veal parmesan
        ~$65</strong>, antipasti $20–$40, pastas $30–$55, main courses $50–$75, sides
        $15–$25, desserts $15–$25. An older official press kit listed appetizers $18–$45
        and mains $37–$120 — treat as dated. Signatures to know:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Spicy Rigatoni Vodka</strong> — the dish that made Carbone famous.</li>
        <li><strong>Veal Parmesan</strong> — the red-sauce canon, elevated.</li>
        <li><strong>Chicken Scarpariello</strong> — sweet-and-sour peppers, sausage, chicken.</li>
        <li><strong>Lobster Fra Diavola</strong> — the luxury pasta move.</li>
        <li><strong>Octopus Pizzaiolo</strong> — the seafood starter people talk about.</li>
        <li><strong>Tableside Caesar salad</strong> — prepared at the table, old-school showmanship.</li>
        <li><strong>Bananas foster flambé</strong> and the <strong>tableside vintage-rum cart</strong> — the sweet finish (rare rums, including vintage Appleton).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The room &amp; the wine</h2>
      <p>
        Ken Fulk's design leans hard into mid-century Italian-American glamour — red leather,
        warm light, tuxedoed service. The wine list runs to some 550 labels with vintages
        back to 1929. This is a see-and-be-seen room where the theater is part of what
        you're paying for.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Non-negotiable:</strong> the spicy rigatoni vodka — it's the signature for a reason.</li>
        <li><strong>The classic:</strong> veal parmesan — the dish that defines the genre.</li>
        <li><strong>To start:</strong> the octopus pizzaiolo or the tableside Caesar.</li>
        <li><strong>To finish:</strong> the bananas foster flambé — and ask about the rum cart.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book ~30 days out</strong> — this is routinely one of the Strip's toughest tables. Reserve through the ARIA site's reservation flow or call +1 (702) 590-2663.</li>
        <li><strong>Not on OpenTable's booking network</strong> — OpenTable's own listing says to contact the restaurant directly (its page carries reviews only).</li>
        <li><strong>Dinner only</strong>, and expect a lively, loud, celebratory room — this is not the quiet fine-dining pick.</li>
        <li><strong>Prices are reported, not published</strong> — the figures above are mid-2025 reports; verify current prices when you book.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://aria.mgmresorts.com/en/restaurants/carbone.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — ARIA</a> (reservations and current hours)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.opentable.com/carbone-las-vegas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenTable listing</a> (reviews; not bookable — reserve via ARIA)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        The restaurant <strong>publishes no current menu prices</strong>. Figures above
        (spicy rigatoni ~$36, veal parm ~$65, pasta/main/side/dessert bands) come from
        <strong>mid-2025 public reporting</strong>; the older press-kit bands ($18–$120)
        are dated further back. Always verify current prices with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More Las Vegas guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-nevada/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in Nevada →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/jean-georges-steakhouse-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Jean Georges Steakhouse at Aria</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— the steakhouse in the same hotel</span></li>
        <li><a href="/nobu-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Nobu at Caesars Palace</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Japanese fine dining from a global name</span></li>
        <li><a href="/sw-steakhouse-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">SW Steakhouse at Wynn</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— the lake-view steakhouse alternative</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
